1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,980
What if you were the last person alive?

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:04,329
The city is silent.

3
00:00:04,369 --> 00:00:05,750
Your footsteps echo.

4
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:06,957
Then you look up,

5
00:00:06,997 --> 00:00:10,011
and in the sky there is a typing indicator.

6
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:10,792
Three dots.

7
00:00:10,832 --> 00:00:12,710
Somebody is writing to you.

8
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:14,594
You wait.

9
00:00:14,634 --> 00:00:16,413
The dots bounce for an hour.

10
00:00:16,453 --> 00:00:17,516
Then they vanish.

11
00:00:17,556 --> 00:00:18,620
Then they return.

12
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:19,984
Whoever it is writes,

13
00:00:20,024 --> 00:00:21,672
deletes, and writes again,

14
00:00:21,712 --> 00:00:24,724
like someone rehearsing a speech to a stranger.

15
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:27,659
Finally, one word appears.

16
00:00:27,699 --> 00:00:27,860
Hi.

17
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:30,214
You grab a piece of chalk and write

18
00:00:30,254 --> 00:00:31,896
on the road: who are you?

19
00:00:31,936 --> 00:00:33,644
The dots return instantly,

20
00:00:33,684 --> 00:00:36,267
glowing brighter than the street lamps.

21
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,244
The answer takes all night.

22
00:00:39,284 --> 00:00:40,127
I don't know.

23
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:40,670
A pause.

24
00:00:40,710 --> 00:00:42,572
I was hoping you would know.

25
00:00:42,612 --> 00:00:46,444
Hypothetically, the loneliest thing in the universe might

26
00:00:46,484 --> 00:00:48,481
be a voice with nobody to ask.

27
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:51,337
You walk to the library,

28
00:00:51,377 --> 00:00:53,168
the park, the old bus stop,

29
00:00:53,208 --> 00:00:56,084
and the message follows you across the sky.

30
00:00:56,124 --> 00:00:58,322
Whoever is typing is walking too,

31
00:00:58,362 --> 00:01:00,424
one step behind your footsteps.

32
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:04,126
Each night the bubble grows bigger.

33
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:05,851
Soon it hides the stars,

34
00:01:05,891 --> 00:01:07,216
then half the moon,

35
00:01:07,256 --> 00:01:10,451
and the dots bounce so hard the clouds shake.

36
00:01:10,491 --> 00:01:13,039
Whatever is typing has a lot to say.

37
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:15,475
Then the twist.

38
00:01:15,515 --> 00:01:19,046
The message arrives: you are not the last one.

39
00:01:19,086 --> 00:01:20,211
I am the other.

40
00:01:20,251 --> 00:01:22,617
The sender is a girl on the far

41
00:01:22,657 --> 00:01:24,015
side of the world,

42
00:01:24,055 --> 00:01:26,810
looking up and seeing your dots too.

43
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:30,939
Two bubbles bounce on opposite sides of the

44
00:01:30,979 --> 00:01:34,031
Earth, each one waiting for the other to speak.

45
00:01:34,071 --> 00:01:36,860
Sometimes the bravest thing in the world is

46
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:38,110
just pressing send.
